{"title":"Oakheart Treant","html":"<article class=\"wp\"><div class=\"wp-main\"><p class=\"wp-lede\">A level 26 Treant that attacks with crush (melee).</p>\n      <h2>Fighting it</h2><div class=\"s\"><i>Weak</i> <span class=\"tag-chip weak\">slash</span><span class=\"tag-chip weak\">burn</span></div>\n      <p class=\"s muted\">A weakness adds 15% damage (the game's own rule). Monsters have no resistances.</p>\n      <p class=\"s good\">⭐ Seen as an elite 1 times (0.7% of sightings). Elites have 3× HP, hit 1.4× harder, give 5× XP and 5× loot.</p>\n      <p class=\"s\">Special: regrowthFracPerSec: .015</p>\n      <h2>Levels</h2><div class=\"q-picker\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Level\"><a class=\"q-chip on\" href=\"#/monster/oakheart-treant\">All levels</a><a class=\"q-chip\" href=\"#/monster/oakheart-treant?lv=21\">Lv 21 <span>58</span></a><a class=\"q-chip\" href=\"#/monster/oakheart-treant?lv=22\">Lv 22 <span>96</span></a><a class=\"q-chip\" href=\"#/monster/oakheart-treant?lv=23\">Lv 23 <span>41</span></a><a class=\"q-chip\" href=\"#/monster/oakheart-treant?lv=26\">Lv 26 <span>2</span></a></div>\n      <p class=\"s muted\">The same monster spawns at different levels, and its hitpoints, damage and XP follow its level (the game’s own formula). In the game a monster more than 5 levels above you shows its level as “???”.</p>\n      <div class=\"g-scroll\"><table class=\"g-table q-table\"><thead><tr><th>Level</th><th>HP</th><th>Damage</th><th>XP</th><th>Elite (HP · dmg · XP)</th><th>Seen</th><th>Mostly</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=\"\" data-href=\"#/monster/oakheart-treant?lv=21\" title=\"Pick level 21\"><td><b>21</b></td><td>70</td><td>16.1</td><td>1,050</td><td class=\"muted\">210 · 22.5 · 3,150</td><td>58</td><td>near <a href=\"#/map/place/Wolfden\">Wolfden</a></td></tr><tr class=\"\" data-href=\"#/monster/oakheart-treant?lv=22\" title=\"Pick level 22\"><td><b>22</b></td><td>74</td><td>16.6</td><td>1,100</td><td class=\"muted\">222 · 23.2 · 3,300</td><td>96</